      "side": 1,
      "message": "Done, the script is vendored verbatim at tests/tools/configure_cluster.sh and the custom wiring is gone (cluster.py drops from 395 to 258 lines).\n\n\n(Extra info)\n------------\nTwo things worth noting: the CONTROLLERIPS quoting bug that netconf patches at runtime was fixed upstream between scripts 13.0.2 and 13.0.4 - 13.0.5 uses IFS\u003d\u0027, \u0027 read -ra, which splits correctly. Our distribution ships sal-clustering-config 13.0.5, so the vendored copy is byte-identical to upstream with no patching at all, which should make a future switch to inheriting it straightforward.\n\nThe script also derives the distribution from its own path (CONTROLLER_DIR\u003d$(dirname $(dirname $0))), so it is copied into each member\u0027s bin/ before being run. It then seeds the three config files itself and sets hostname, roles, seed-nodes and shard replicas, so _pin_pekko_canonical_hostname and the HOCON editing could all be removed.",
      "parentUuid": "320338b9_37e57ebd",
